From 746a1e737f7a32447a8ba8e124ccdbe723e5ab7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 03:30:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvk/rm, wsi: block-linear Win32 scanout swapchains with
 NVIDIA's modifier

Patch 0021 presents swapchain images by host scanout with no copy to a
window, but the images are linear, and NVK cannot render into linear
color images: every render pass draws into a hidden tiled shadow and
copies it into the linear image (nvk_cmd_draw.c, linear_tiled_shadows),
so each frame still has a full-screen GPU copy plus the shadow's VRAM.

Now the images keep NVK's own tiling, named by NVIDIA's DRM format
modifier, which the host's display path reads as such (verified on the
host with NVIDIA's driver importing NVK-on-RM block-linear memory,
spike/host-nvk-import):

vulkan/wsi (Win32):
- The scanout image type asks the driver for its uncompressed NVIDIA
  block-linear 2D modifiers for the format (GetPhysicalDeviceFormat-
  Properties2 + DRM modifier list), keeps those that suit the swapchain's
  usage, flags and extent (GetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2, as
  wsi_common_drm.c does), and creates the images with
  VK_IMAGE_TILING_DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER_EXT and that list.  The driver
  picks (NVK: the tallest block, h = 5, 0x0300000000606015 for
  B8G8R8A8 on GB20x).  None left: LINEAR, as before.
- scanout_export now takes the image and returns the modifier the image
  got (vkGetImageDrmFormatModifierPropertiesEXT is Linux-only in the
  runtime); the present names it in the flip instead of LINEAR.
- wsi_device::win32.scanout_linear: LINEAR images only.  The driver sets
  it at init (NVK_HELIOS_WSI_LINEAR=1); the WSI sets it itself when a
  flip comes back VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED (the display path refused
  the modifier) and returns VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR, so the application
  recreates the swapchain, linear.

nvk/rm (Windows):
- The dedicated allocation of a DRM-modifier image already takes the
  image's PTE kind and tile mode (nvk_AllocateMemory), and the export
  already passes them to NVKMS as block-linear surface params on
  DRM_NVIDIA_GEM_IMPORT_NVKMS_MEMORY (log2GobsPerBlock.y from the tile
  mode, genericMemory), as nvkmd_rm_drm.c does on Linux.  The export
  now checks that the memory's layout is the modifier's (generic kind =
  the modifier's kind, block height = h, no depth blocks; LINEAR: no
  kind) and refuses otherwise, so the swapchain falls back.
- A SCANOUT_SET refused with -EINVAL (layout the KMD does not forward)
  for a non-linear modifier is VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED, the WSI's
  signal to go linear.  KMD 22.22.308..310 validates size, fourcc and
  stride only, so block-linear modifiers pass.
